  into a project-scoped lore directory. See docs/project-scope.md for what "project scope"
  means and how it differs from a global lore directory shared across projects.
-->

## Project knowledge base (lore)

This project keeps a local, agent-maintained knowledge base under `lore/` (gitignored; see
`docs/templates/project-gitignore.snippet`). Before working on an unfamiliar subsystem, read
`lore/index.md` for the list of pages, then the specific page that covers it. `lore/index.md`
is an index: it points at pages, it does not duplicate their content.

After learning something about this project that is not obvious from the code or git
history (a design decision, a constraint, a gotcha), record it as a new or updated page under
`lore/pages/`, following `lore/schema.md`, then rebuild the index:

```bash
python3 <path-to-lore>/scripts/lore.py index --lore-dir lore
```

Do not duplicate a fact that is already clear from reading the code itself; lore is for
context the code cannot show on its own.
